WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.152
In the Eastern Han there was a famous scholar named Zhang Heng. At night, he often gazed up at the starry sky, observing the heavens.

00:00:10.152 --> 00:00:19.632
Zhang Heng designed a magical instrument called the seismoscope, which could tell from which direction an earthquake came.

00:00:19.632 --> 00:00:28.080
Following his design, the craftsmen poured molten bronze into molds and at last cast the instrument.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:39.744
The seismoscope looked like a great wine vessel, with eight dragons on top, each holding a bronze ball in its mouth, and eight toads below.

00:00:39.744 --> 00:00:49.272
One day the ground suddenly shook, and the bronze ball in one dragon's mouth dropped into a toad's mouth.

00:00:49.272 --> 00:00:57.864
Zhang Heng pointed in the direction of the fallen ball and announced loudly that the earthquake had come from there — and the officials were utterly amazed!

